{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And Moses said to his father-in-law: Because the people come to me to inquire of Elohim.</b> For whoever wishes to know the reason for a judgment given to him, even if there were a hundred judges sitting with me in court, he would never come except to me, to inquire of Elohim — that is to say, the judgments of HaShem — and I have no room to exempt myself from their cry. And if you would say: if so, you should have withheld yourself from judging entirely and appointed others, and you would thereby cut off their complaint against you — concerning this he said, ״כִּי יִהְיֶה לָהֶם דָּבָר בָּא אֵלַי״ — it does not say בָּאוּ אֵלַי, but it refers to that matter itself, for the matter comes to me through prophecy, and everything is in the hand of HaShem; He granted me insight, and every hidden matter in which there are no witnesses — that matter comes to me, so that I have the power to judge between a man and his fellow, that is, in matters between them in which there are no witnesses; therefore it is not fitting for me to evade the judging. And perhaps it is concerning this that he said, ״וְהַדָּבָר אֲשֶׁר יִקְשֶׁה מִכֶּם תַּקְרִיבוּן אֵלַי וּשְׁמַעְתִּיו״ (Deuteronomy 1:17) — that is, in a case where there are no witnesses in the matter, you shall bring them to me and I will hear it from the mouth of the Omnipotent. And Jethro said to him: even so, ״לֹא טוֹב הַדָּבָר אֲשֶׁר אַתָּה עֹשֶׂה״ — and he did not say here ״לָעָם״ as he wrote above, because he told him that what you are doing is not good both for yourself and for the people, ״כִּי נָבֹל תִּבּוֹל גַּם אַתָּה גַּם הָעָם״, for ״כָבֵד מִמְּךָ הַדָּבָר״, and you need to lighten their complaint from upon yourself." "Another interpretation: <b>When they have a matter, it comes to me.</b> One of them — that is, the claimant comes to me alone in order to arrange his arguments before me, and I do not listen to his words, but rather ״וְשָׁפַטְתִּי בֵּין אִישׁ וּבֵין רֵעֵהוּ״ — only when the two of them are standing before me specifically."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:21:15.677199247Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}